# Screen reader — « Lecteur d'écran » (Paramètres > Accessibilité > Lecteur d'écran, Super+Alt+S; backend
# shell/main/ipc/screenreader.js, session side shell/renderer/core/features/screenreader.js).
# Orca runs for the session user and reads the shell, its apps and web pages over AT-SPI (the shell turns Chromium
# accessibility on while it runs). It speaks through speech-dispatcher with the espeak-ng module, in the UI language:
# espeak-ng-data carries the French voice (fr, fr-be, fr-ch) and every other language.
# speech-dispatcher runs per user (its user socket, enabled globally by the package and by build.sh); the system-wide
# speech-dispatcherd.service stays disabled. at-spi2-core's bus is D-Bus activated in the session.
# gsettings (libglib2.0-bin + dconf) carries org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications screen-reader-enabled, which
# at-spi-bus-launcher mirrors to apps and Orca watches to quit.
orca
speech-dispatcher
speech-dispatcher-espeak-ng
python3-speechd
espeak-ng
espeak-ng-data
at-spi2-core
gsettings-desktop-schemas
libglib2.0-bin
dconf-gsettings-backend
dconf-service
